[{'caption': 'Thank you all so much for the support on my previous reel, and let’s continue advocating for the San Joaquin River! I want to clarify that although a 3-3 vote means that the permits were denied by the Fresno County Planning Commission, CEMEX is likely to appeal this ruling within the next 15 days, meaning they will take this fight to our Fresno county Board of Supervisors. Click the link in my bio for information on how YOU can contact our Fresno county Board of Supervisors, in order to voice your concerns with CEMEX’s proposed blast mine. Thank you all for your continued support and inquiry about how to get involved, Let’s keep fighting!', 'datetime': '2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '4003962284021286568', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.71878-15/840697874_3006926756323222_8723924270543703580_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=107&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=ykTSTtoYbAYQ7kNvwEpI7On&_nc_oc=AdqOk5Q4NaZ1EyELfaFG_pEQl5wTG7q8ZudKu15-_K_K3tVQ4twcoa5_OSXEhtijAeA&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQSbp8AOaf1kfNZxxAvd3Or0oB1zoiKDYZavvyBnBsm0LA&oe=6AED6436', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Video', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DeQ7nvBJoao'}, {'caption': 'UPDATE: With a 3-3 vote, the Fresno County planning commission denied approval for the permits required in order for CEMEX to expand operations at the Rockfield site. This, however does NOT mean the fight is over, as CEMEX is likely to appeal within the next 15 days. This means that we will likely see this proposal heard by the Fresno County Board of Supervisors. As a result, it’s critical that within then next 15 days we continue lobbying against CEMEX by sending emails to the Fresno County Board of Directors, regarding our concerns with the project. Click the link in my bio to learn more about how to contact the members of our counties’ board of supervisors, and for more updates on CEMEX’s appeal. Thank you all for your continued support of the San Joaquin River, and the preservation of our water for generations to come! Let’s keep fighting!', 'datetime': '2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '4002563075346984701', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/839010462_18226577503334821_2892332141912505379_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=111&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=Sy9g_CM7GmQQ7kNvwE2e7qL&_nc_oc=AdriQQvuvmCYeWVlxihGIEAUWAyzvEDz67pnjSTvGVxyTdmreQRJeYsxecIDS8vacNc&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQTiXmaDptVujXJgl49niisPlLDX9lMCkFLfSaes25zuFw&oe=6AED433A', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Video', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DeL9ekZJu79'}, {'caption': 'Spent an incredible 5 days exploring an entirely new world I never knew existed.

The Florida Everglades are still calling my name, even as I settle back into the normalcy of my life in California.  I experienced so much beauty and depth within this incredible ecosystem, and in that way I think it goes without saying I will absolutely be returning to this incredible place within the next year. 

Special thanks to the amazing @lucamartinez.fl for the hospitality and showing me around your backyard!', 'datetime': '2026-05-29T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3907945172381538715', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/708979093_18212538529334821_1615850133284562718_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0FST1VTRUxfSVRFTS5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=vdpSJyS8WP4Q7kNvwHfx5RS&_nc_oc=AdrzjjVRM-T5o5wJoo3HJ87SooXoQ0rlJFyMjC92EYEEkXmRstAV8cKGDMueOr5qGR4&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQSsoHWCoyTyngeqtGrhIKsP2t9aXhVOqH58HhVCwGREHg&oe=6AED4943', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Carousel', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DY7z23ZgRmb'}, {'caption': 'St. Augustine 🌋 

Recently in the past 2 weeks as I’ve looked back upon my trip to Alaska, I’ve realized how much I’ve missed not only the amazing friends and wildlife, but also the gorgeous snow capped peaks that line the coast and interior of the Alaskan peninsula. This shot features one of the larger geological formations in the area, the st. Augustine volcano. As our group watched this mama bear and her cub rest under the stormy clouds above, we couldn’t help but notice the perfect alignment of the two bears with the gorgeous face of the volcano. I enjoy how this shot shows a small percent of our he gorgeous geography we were treated with during our trip', 'datetime': '2025-07-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3667492279469730620', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/514553187_18176459017334821_2303675447643962252_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=5PyJpYds0mAQ7kNvwGsbu4T&_nc_oc=AdpYTnQWdndvMFpKgaDv-QteHp3zgJA9nuclYa8A6iHIyCEcbgDiVYbw5CJkmb83jKs&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQQ7mA4N8k_hxZWHy-Z2IviDta6GS1CThl9PjTwBWtz2rA&oe=6AED47B2', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Image', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DLljMwGR-s8'}, {'caption': 'In the words of @toddnet “that’s badass…”

As this Boar Grizzly stood up from its deep slumber in a tidal ditch, it began to make its way towards our group. Mouth agape, slobber dripping, and an intent gaze fixed upon us, but its body language showed no indication of aggression, but instead that of curiosity. It stopped a mere 20 feet away, and with 2 drawn out breaths began unleashing the urine built up in what seemed to be a drunken stooper. It unleashed this flash flood of pee for over a minute and a half, as our group struggled to hold in our laughter at the absurdity of what was unfolding in front of us. Shortly after, the bear made its way across the mudflats to resume its feeding, and many fist bumps and smiles were shared as we prepared to return to the lodge.', 'datetime': '2025-06-29T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3665937540810854493', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.75761-15/515081637_18176259049334821_3765975966516816095_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=104&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=URwsgw1dQhIQ7kNvwGq1OYy&_nc_oc=AdqKgNWK1z_OuZWLQub2CZkdYORduuzolZ1syyZRgYV4ZxdqQsJWhZhHhTTuq73E1Yk&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQQSwgG49VtwKr98_t-cacgw0RFeWQHbCMjsU7-JusrTcA&oe=6AED6D6A', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Image', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DLgBsU4zNBd'}, {'caption': 'Grizzly 🐻 

A little over a week ago, I had the immense pleasure of joining 9 other like minded wildlife passionate creatives for the trip of a life time in the Alaskan bush for a week of incredible shooting, conversations, and relationships built. 

I could’ve never imagined 6 years ago when I first joined this app that I would be meeting people my age from all across the country who shared the same passion and eye for nature as I did, and I’m so blessed that @gary.farber.photo and @toddnet  were gracious enough to allow me to be a part of this once in a lifetime trip. 

As you may have noticed through my lack of posting, wildlife photography has been on the back burner in my life for quite some time, however spending every single day of such a special week with some of the most talented and intelligent individuals I have ever met has not only given me hope for the future of conservation through photography, but also re-sparked the flame that once brought me to nature and capturing special moments.

Forever grateful to the following people for making this such an incredible trip!

@gary.farber.photo 
@toddnet 
@lucamartinez.fl 
@mattpoolephoto 
@sorengoldsmith 
@maceo.susi 
@calebg.hoover 
@john.d.gidney 
@joshhauge_photography', 'datetime': '2025-06-26T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3663785055148687094', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.75761-15/513821977_18175976011334821_4549796433174265814_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=100&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=ZSiutHa7tNkQ7kNvwG5Garg&_nc_oc=AdouZ-z0aFoMs82CjPUok2h4S9t1RMtXJQB_T5WvejKCUGgkQh6XBDAqRv-Caqip7xY&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQQyRHZKWJj472xvRKBwOkK_nAsYN1boSHfbdVOvqc7Llw&oe=6AED60C9', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Image', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DLYYRiZhb72'}, {'caption': 'Forest gnome 🧙‍♂️

The sun hits the back of the tree line and my hope for finding a great grey that night fades with the dying light. Hours of searching has made any small inconsistency in trees has made my bird sense fire. Despite my weary eyes, there is no mistaking the shape of a great grey. There was no imagining as my eyes locked onto the dark silhouette standing out from the vibrant greens of the meadow. As soon as I hopped out of the car I slinked my way to the edge of the meadow and was treated with the best moments of my time as a wildlife photographer. 30 minutes spent in near darkness with natures most mysterious predator. I hope you enjoy 

