Recently in the past 2 weeks as I’ve looked back upon my trip to Alaska, I’ve realized how much I’ve missed not only the amazing friends and wildlife, but also the gorgeous snow capped peaks that line the coast and interior of the Alaskan peninsula. This shot features one of the larger geological formations in the area, the st. Augustine volcano. As our group watched this mama bear and her cub rest under the stormy clouds above, we couldn’t help but notice the perfect alignment of the two bears with the gorgeous face of the volcano. I enjoy how this shot shows a small percent of our he gorgeous geography we were treated with during our trip', 'datetime': '2025-07-01T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3667492279469730620', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/514553187_18176459017334821_2303675447643962252_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=5PyJpYds0mAQ7kNvwGsbu4T&_nc_oc=AdpYTnQWdndvMFpKgaDv-QteHp3zgJA9nuclYa8A6iHIyCEcbgDiVYbw5CJkmb83jKs&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQQ7mA4N8k_hxZWHy-Z2IviDta6GS1CThl9PjTwBWtz2rA&oe=6AED47B2', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Image', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DLljMwGR-s8'}, {'caption': 'In the words of @toddnet “that’s badass…”

As this Boar Grizzly stood up from its deep slumber in a tidal ditch, it began to make its way towards our group. Mouth agape, slobber dripping, and an intent gaze fixed upon us, but its body language showed no indication of aggression, but instead that of curiosity. It stopped a mere 20 feet away, and with 2 drawn out breaths began unleashing the urine built up in what seemed to be a drunken stooper. It unleashed this flash flood of pee for over a minute and a half, as our group struggled to hold in our laughter at the absurdity of what was unfolding in front of us. Shortly after, the bear made its way across the mudflats to resume its feeding, and many fist bumps and smiles were shared as we prepared to return to the lodge.', 'datetime': '2025-06-29T00:00:00.000Z', 'id': '3665937540810854493', 'image_url': 'https://scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.75761-15/515081637_18176259049334821_3765975966516816095_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=104&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=URwsgw1dQhIQ7kNvwGq1OYy&_nc_oc=AdqKgNWK1z_OuZWLQub2CZkdYORduuzolZ1syyZRgYV4ZxdqQsJWhZhHhTTuq73E1Yk&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=edoj170g6OQKhVhIIAy_lg&_nc_ss=7a689&oh=00_AQQSwgG49VtwKr98_t-cacgw0RFeWQHbCMjsU7-JusrTcA&oe=6AED6D6A', 'post_hashtags': None, 'content_type': 'Image', 'url': 'https://www.instagram.com/p/DLgBsU4zNBd'}, {'caption': 'Grizzly 🐻 

A little over a week ago, I had the immense pleasure of joining 9 other like minded wildlife passionate creatives for the trip of a life time in the Alaskan bush for a week of incredible shooting, conversations, and relationships built. 

I could’ve never imagined 6 years ago when I first joined this app that I would be meeting people my age from all across the country who shared the same passion and eye for nature as I did, and I’m so blessed that @gary.farber.photo and @toddnet  were gracious enough to allow me to be a part of this once in a lifetime trip. 

As you may have noticed through my lack of posting, wildlife photography has been on the back burner in my life for quite some time, however spending every single day of such a special week with some of the most talented and intelligent individuals I have ever met has not only given me hope for the future of conservation through photography, but also re-sparked the flame that once brought me to nature and capturing special moments.

Forever grateful to the following people for making this such an incredible trip!

