The sun hits the back of the tree line and my hope for finding a great grey that night fades with the dying light. Hours of searching has made any small inconsistency in trees has made my bird sense fire. Despite my weary eyes, there is no mistaking the shape of a great grey. There was no imagining as my eyes locked onto the dark silhouette standing out from the vibrant greens of the meadow. As soon as I hopped out of the car I slinked my way to the edge of the meadow and was treated with the best moments of my time as a wildlife photographer. 30 minutes spent in near darkness with natures most mysterious predator. I hope you enjoy 

