While searching through dense comfier thickets high and low for any evidence of possibly nesting activity, my mom sends me a message. A ping in my pocket caused me to jump, but I quickly realized it was the buzz of my phone. Opening up my phone I immediately see a photo sent by my mom 5 minutes prior (I was out of service). The photo showed a very blurry figure stop a branch mere feet off the ground. Instantly walking to the trail she had gone walking down and I was able to spot her sitting on some fallen logs. She motioned to a tree 70 feet or so from our current location. The tall stature of the great grey blended in so well despite its size! I carefully crept along the forest floor in the birds direction, looking at the bird every few steps to check it’s behavior. Eventually the bird took off, but to my surprise it was flying towards me! It landed on this young conifer tree and allowed me to watch as it scanned the forest floor for a potential meal. Eventually this bird dove down to a stump on the forest floor and took off to hunt elsewhere. It was amazing to see one of these birds hunting in the forest so close!

