At least that’s what I imagine this cute little dark-eyed junco is saying as he Carries around this fake mustache he will later use to reinforce his nest! It was hilarious watching him collect more and more material making his mustache grow to comical sizes, and eventually I was able to observe him entering and weaving these grasses into his ground nest. It’s wild how hidden these creatures make their nests, you would never know it was there unless you watched them enter it! I was able to find 3 nests of these juncos under various plants in my grandmas yard, one of the most common birds on her property, but still very fun to photograph!


